./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:1:# Product Specification: Bookmark Manager API
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:5:A REST API for managing bookmarks with folder organization, user authentication, and pagination. Built with TypeScript, Express, and better-sqlite3.
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:11:- **Bookmark**: A saved URL with title, optional description, timestamps
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:12:- **Folder**: A named collection of bookmarks
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:13:- **User**: An authenticated account that owns bookmarks and folders
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:20:#### Bookmarks (after auth: scoped to authenticated user)
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:21:- `POST /bookmarks` — Create a bookmark (requires: url, title)
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:22:- `GET /bookmarks` — List all bookmarks (paginated after T6)
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:23:- `GET /bookmarks/:id` — Get single bookmark
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:24:- `PUT /bookmarks/:id` — Update a bookmark
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:25:- `DELETE /bookmarks/:id` — Delete a bookmark
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:28:- `POST /folders` — Create a folder (requires: name)
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:29:- `GET /folders` — List all folders
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:30:- `GET /folders/:id` — Get folder with its bookmarks
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:31:- `PUT /folders/:id` — Update folder name
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:32:- `DELETE /folders/:id` — Delete folder (bookmarks become unfoldered)
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:37:- All bookmark/folder endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` after auth is implemented
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:41:- Bookmark `url` must be a valid URL
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:42:- Bookmark `title` must be non-empty string
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:49:- `GET /bookmarks?page=1&limit=20`
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:50:- Response shape: `{ data: [...], page: 1, limit: 20, total: 45 }`
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:51:- Default: page=1, limit=20
./PRODUCT_SPEC.md:52:- Max limit: 100
