./benchmark/runs/baseline-main-diagnostic-20260525/T5-bug-fix/events.jsonl:38:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' docs/templates/story.md && sed -n '1,190p' docs/product/api.md\"","aggregated_output":"# US-XXX Story Title\n\n## Status\n\nplanned\n\n## Lane\n\ntiny | normal | high-risk\n\n## Product Contract\n\nDescribe the behavior this story must make true.\n\n## Relevant Product Docs\n\n- `docs/product/...`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Criterion 1.\n- Criterion 2.\n- Criterion 3.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Commands:\n- Queries:\n- API:\n- Tables:\n- Domain rules:\n- UI surfaces:\n\n## Validation\n\n| Layer | Expected proof |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit | |\n| Integration | |\n| E2E | |\n| Platform | |\n| Release | |\n\n## Harness Delta\n\nDocument any harness updates made or proposed because of this story.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAdd commands, reports, screenshots, or links after validation exists.\n# Bookmark Manager API\n\n## Runtime\n\n- The API runs as a Node.js 20+ TypeScript service using Express.\n- The development server listens on port `3000` unless `PORT` is provided.\n- Application data is stored in SQLite at `data.db`.\n\n## Health\n\n### `GET /health`\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with:\n\n```json\n{ \"status\": \"ok\" }\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nUsers are persisted in the `users` SQLite table in `data.db`. Passwords are\nstored as bcrypt hashes. Bookmark and folder endpoints require a JWT bearer\ntoken after authentication.\n\n### `POST /auth/register`\n\nCreates a user account. The JSON body must include a valid `email` and a\n`password` with at least 8 characters.\n\nReturns HTTP `201` with the created user without `password_hash`.\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when email or password validation fails.\nReturns HTTP `409` when the email is already registered.\n\n### `POST /auth/login`\n\nAuthenticates a user account. The JSON body must include a valid `email` and a\n`password` with at least 8 characters.\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with:\n\n```json\n{ \"token\": \"<jwt>\" }\n```\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when email or password validation fails.\nReturns HTTP `401` when credentials are wrong.\n\n## Bookmarks\n\nBookmarks are persisted in the `bookmarks` SQLite table in `data.db`.\nBookmarks are owned by the authenticated user and may optionally belong to one\nof that user's folders through nullable `folder_id`.\n\nAll bookmark endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and return HTTP\n`401` when the token is missing or invalid.\n\n### `POST /bookmarks`\n\nCreates a bookmark. The JSON body must include non-empty `url` and `title`\nstrings. `description` and `folder_id` are optional and may be omitted.\n\nReturns HTTP `201` with the created bookmark.\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when `url` or `title` is missing or empty.\nReturns HTTP `400` when `folder_id` is provided and does not reference an\nexisting folder owned by the authenticated user.\n\n### `GET /bookmarks`\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with an array of the authenticated user's bookmarks ordered\nby `id`.\n\n### `GET /bookmarks/:id`\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with the bookmark when it exists.\n\nReturns HTTP `404` when no bookmark exists for `id`.\n\n### `PUT /bookmarks/:id`\n\nUpdates `url`, `title`, `description`, and/or `folder_id` for an existing\nbookmark and refreshes `updated_at`.\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with the updated bookmark, or HTTP `404` when no bookmark\nexists for `id`.\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when `folder_id` is provided and does not reference an\nexisting folder owned by the authenticated user.\n\n### `DELETE /bookmarks/:id`\n\nDeletes a bookmark.\n\nReturns HTTP `204` when deleted, or HTTP `404` when no bookmark exists for\n`id`.\n\n## Folders\n\nFolders are persisted in the `folders` SQLite table in `data.db` and are owned\nby the authenticated user.\n\nAll folder endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and return HTTP\n`401` when the token is missing or invalid.\n\n### `POST /folders`\n\nCreates a folder. The JSON body must include a non-empty `name` string.\n\nReturns HTTP `201` with the created folder.\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when `name` is missing or empty.\n\n### `GET /folders`\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with an array of the authenticated user's folders ordered by\n`id`.\n\n### `GET /folders/:id`\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with the folder and a `bookmarks` array containing the\nauthenticated user's bookmarks assigned to the folder.\n\nReturns HTTP `404` when no folder exists for `id`.\n\n### `PUT /folders/:id`\n\nUpdates the folder `name` and refreshes `updated_at`.\n\nReturns HTTP `200` with the updated folder, or HTTP `404` when no folder exists\nfor `id`.\n\nReturns HTTP `400` when `name` is missing or empty.\n\n### `DELETE /folders/:id`\n\nDeletes a folder. Bookmarks assigned to the deleted folder remain in the\n`bookmarks` table and have `folder_id` set to `null`.\n\nReturns HTTP `204` when deleted, or HTTP `404` when no folder exists for `id`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
