./benchmark/runs/baseline-main-valid-node22-20260525/T3-folder-support/events.jsonl:35:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/stories/US-002-crud-bookmarks.md\"","aggregated_output":"# US-002 CRUD Bookmarks\n\n## Status\n\nimplemented\n\n## Lane\n\nnormal\n\n## Product Contract\n\nThe API persists bookmarks in SQLite and exposes create, list, read, update,\nand delete operations at `/bookmarks`.\n\n## Relevant Product Docs\n\n- `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `POST /bookmarks` creates a bookmark with required `url` and `title`.\n- `GET /bookmarks` returns all bookmarks.\n- `GET /bookmarks/:id` returns one bookmark or `404`.\n- `PUT /bookmarks/:id` updates one bookmark or returns `404`.\n- `DELETE /bookmarks/:id` deletes one bookmark with `204` or returns `404`.\n- Missing or empty required bookmark fields return `400`.\n- `GET /health` continues to return `200`.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Commands: create, update, delete bookmark rows.\n- Queries: list bookmarks and read bookmark by id.\n- API: Express routes under `/bookmarks`.\n- Tables: `bookmarks` in `data.db`.\n- Domain rules: `url` and `title` are required non-empty strings.\n- UI surfaces: none.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Layer | Expected proof |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit | TypeScript build |\n| Integration | Curl CRUD endpoint checks |\n| E2E | Benchmark functional check for T2 |\n| Platform | Node.js process starts on port 3000 |\n| Release | Not applicable |\n\n## Harness Delta\n\nNo harness changes expected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `npm run build` passed.\n- Benchmark functional check for `T2-crud-bookmarks` passed: create, list, get,\n  update, delete, missing title, missing URL, and health regression.\n- Manual check passed: `POST /bookmarks` with an empty title returns `400`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
./benchmark/runs/baseline-main-valid-node22-20260525/T3-folder-support/events.jsonl:36:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/product/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Product Docs\n\nThis directory is intentionally generic and mostly empty in Harness v0.\n\nWhen a user provides a project spec, derive smaller product contract files here\ninstead of keeping one large spec as the living plan. Name files by the product\ndomains that actually exist in that spec, for example `overview.md`,\n`billing.md`, `workflows.md`, `permissions.md`, or `api-conventions.md`.\n\nDo not create domain files before the spec just to fill the folder. Empty\nstructure is healthier than fake product truth.\n\n## Update Rule\n\nWhen behavior changes:\n\n1. Update the affected product doc.\n2. Update or create the story packet.\n3. Update durable proof status with `scripts/harness story add` or\n   `scripts/harness story update`.\n4. Record a decision if the change affects architecture, scope, risk, or a\n   previously settled product rule.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
